ate from our  existing resources now this is very cool  so if you have a development environment  you could launch cloud format to create  a template from your existing resources  so that you can just press a button to  duplicate it whenever you need to it's  what we're going to do is we're going to  take a look at create a stack so we'll  click on that and we can either design  our own or we can choose a template so  we're going to use that and you can see  there's a few options here available for  us so what we're going to do is we're  going to do a single instance wordpress  blog and we can take a look at this  in the designer to see what it looks  like so i'm just going to open this up  in a new window okay so let me zoom out  i sort of disappear down here there it  is so this is a very simple cloud  formation template and it's going to  create an ec2 instance which is going to  be our web server which is going to host  the wordpress blog and it's going to  create a security group for us now if  you go down to the bottom we have a look  at the JSON we can see what it's doing  so it's allowing us to create this on in  all of these different instance types  then we have what's going to be allowed  where people can connect from the  database name who the DB user is etc is  there's all sorts of things going on  down there so let me just flip back to  CloudFormation and then we'll go through  the configuration steps okay so we now  click on next and this here is the  graphical representation of the JSON  code so we can give this stack a name so  we're just going to call it test because  we're not actually going to launch this  then the DB name so it's a WordPress DB  and the DB password  we can give it a password if we want to  let's just call it flat for now  DB user so who we want to be able to  connect I'm going to call that admin  then we get to choose the instance type  so we can choose any of these instance  types for our wordpress blog and then we  need to give it the key so we'll use our  simply learn key pair and the SSH  location so what IP range do we want it  to be accessible from an SSH so we could  tighten this down to say chess my IP  address but we're just going to leave it  open then we click on next we get to  give it a tag if we want to and then we  get to the creation stage so we get to  review is telling us it's using this  template as a description of what it  does there's a warning here it says this  template creates an Amazon ec2 instance  and you will be billed to the resources  if you use it now it's worth remembering  some of these cloud formation templates  have some pretty high powered servers  involved in them so when you launch them  you may incur some significant costs so  just be aware of that then you have the  details that we typed in and then when  we're done you just click create and it  would create that stack for you and this  concludes the demonstration for cloud  formation hey once you become an expert  in cloud computing then subscribe to  simply learn Channel and click here to  watch more such videos turner it up and  get certified in cloud computing click  here

